# The broker the workshop uses. Copy this file to broker.env and edit it. Without broker.env, the services and
# cluster/cluster.sh use the local Docker cluster. A RABBITMQ_URL environment variable overrides this file.
#
# RABBITMQ_URL is one URL: amqp://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/VHOST, or amqps:// for TLS. The part after the last / is the
# virtual host (%2F is "/"). The scripts work out everything else from it: a localhost URL without a port means the
# 3 nodes of the local cluster, and cluster/cluster.sh finds the management API at https://HOST for amqps:// URLs and
# at http://HOST:15672 for amqp:// URLs.

# Local cluster (the default)
RABBITMQ_URL=amqp://guest:guest@localhost/%2F

# CloudAMQP: paste the AMQP URL from your instance's details page instead
# RABBITMQ_URL=amqps://USER:PASSWORD@HOST.rmq.cloudamqp.com/VHOST
